From a7b5bb5c2ebd753ac62b0e8ac32172410f8300bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:26:38 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 325/405] Names: a part put into an assembly keeps an ASCII
 name; names are read as UTF-8
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Assembly's "Put Part" named the link after the part's label, so a part
labelled 部品 got the internal name 部品003, and the GUI reads internal
names as Latin-1 in many places: the status bar said "é¨å003" (engine
field tests 0.7.3, 0.7.4), and a lookup by such a name would miss. The
link is named after the part's name (the label stays the part's label),
and the GUI's QString::fromLatin1(getNameInDocument()) and
getObject(...toLatin1()) use UTF-8 (the same for ASCII names).

Tests: TestAssemblySolve, TestAssemblyWorkbench, TestPartDesignApp,
TestSketcherApp, TestSpreadsheet, Document

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
